    "The supervisor control owns and aborts the actual extracted supervisor; cancellation observation precedes closing its retained client. It proves a finite surviving handler if it reaches the intended failure, not a permanent socket leak.",
    "Supervisor accept timeout remains original 300 ms. Cancelled join requires actual cancellation before this bounded supervisor naturally finishes; no scheduling sleep provides readiness.",
    "Partial-next-head control sends malformed bytes only after a literal407/authenticated204 and observes actual connection closure before requiring retained UnexpectedEof. Clean zero EOF is a distinct positive.",
